Ladybird now resolves a numeric line-height to the number times the
computed font size, and a length line-height to its computed length. Run
in Chrome 158 and WebKit 26.5, every case of the test matches Chrome
exactly (15.295px for 1.15 at 13.3px, 38.4px for 38.4px), and WebKit to
within its single-precision digits (19.200001px). Both lay out a
1/64px-rounded line box while they report the unrounded value.
Firefox 151 reports its line box height, which it rounds to its 1/60px
app units (15.3px and 20px, where Chrome gives 15.295px and 19.995px).
